<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document>
<name>Chumphon sidewalk route G2 (10-group plan)</name>
<Style id="g2film"><LineStyle><color>ff4b9d2a</color><width>5</width></LineStyle></Style>
<Style id="g2opt"><LineStyle><color>994b9d2a</color><width>4</width></LineStyle></Style>
<Style id="g2con"><LineStyle><color>ff8a8a8a</color><width>2</width></LineStyle></Style>
<Folder><name>Group 2</name>
<Placemark><name>G2 START</name><description>West end of Rajaveetnai Rd (ถ.ราษฎร์วิถีใน)</description><Point><coordinates>99.1741,10.49417,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G2 step 1: Rajaveetnai Rd (optional)</name><description>Start here. Head east along Rajaveetnai Rd for about 170 m to where it meets Poowanaad Damnurn Rd (ถ.ภูนารถดำเนิน). [Optional / blue - film if time allows]</description><styleUrl>#g2opt</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>99.1741,10.49417,0 99.17434,10.49413,0 99.17468,10.4941,0 99.17476,10.49409,0 99.17494,10.49409,0 99.17512,10.49408,0 99.1754,10.49408,0 99.17563,10.49406,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G2 step 2: Poowanaad Damnurn Rd</name><description>Turn right onto Poowanaad Damnurn Rd (ถ.ภูนารถดำเนิน), heading south for about 90 m to where it meets Riverside walkway along the Tha Taphao River (ทางเดินริมแม่น้ำท่าตะเภา).</description><styleUrl>#g2film</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>99.17563,10.49406,0 99.17554,10.49359,0 99.17552,10.49344,0 99.17555,10.49326,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G2 step 3: Riverside walkway along the Tha Taphao River</name><description>Turn left onto Riverside walkway along the Tha Taphao River (ทางเดินริมแม่น้ำท่าตะเภา), heading east for about 700 m to where it meets East riverbank south of Hwy 327 (check on site first) (ริมตลิ่งฝั่งตะวันออก ใต้ทางหลวง 327). [Mostly not in Google Maps: the first ~420 m hugs the north bank (follow the riverside path on foot); the last ~270 m is the east-bank road down to Hwy 327, which Google does show]</description><styleUrl>#g2film</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>99.17555,10.49326,0 99.17594,10.49324,0 99.1771,10.49389,0 99.17737,10.49389,0 99.17754,10.49382,0 99.17783,10.49361,0 99.17795,10.4934,0 99.17814,10.49235,0 99.1786,10.49191,0 99.17889,10.49149,0 99.1793,10.49118,0 99.17938,10.491,0 99.17936,10.49038,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G2 step 4: East riverbank south of Hwy 327 (check on site first) (optional)</name><description>Continue straight onto East riverbank south of Hwy 327 (check on site first) (ริมตลิ่งฝั่งตะวันออก ใต้ทางหลวง 327), heading south for about 460 m to the next junction. [Optional / blue - film if time allows] [Optional and NOT in Google Maps or OpenStreetMap: check on site first that the east riverbank is walkable; skip it if not]</description><styleUrl>#g2opt</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>99.17936,10.49038,0 99.17976,10.48933,0 99.17983,10.48923,0 99.18081,10.48883,0 99.18156,10.48867,0 99.18206,10.48838,0 99.18222,10.48817,0 99.18221,10.48793,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G2 step 5: East riverbank south of Hwy 327 (check on site first) (optional)</name><description>Bear right to stay on East riverbank south of Hwy 327 (check on site first) (ริมตลิ่งฝั่งตะวันออก ใต้ทางหลวง 327), heading south-west for about 270 m to the finish point. [Optional / blue - film if time allows] [Optional and NOT in Google Maps or OpenStreetMap: check on site first that the east riverbank is walkable; skip it if not]</description><styleUrl>#g2opt</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>99.18221,10.48793,0 99.18198,10.48741,0 99.18162,10.4869,0 99.18121,10.48647,0 99.18098,10.48609,0 99.18075,10.48597,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>G2 FINISH</name><description>End of the east-riverbank stretch, about 700 m south of the Hwy 327 river bridge</description><Point><coordinates>99.18075,10.48597,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder>
</Document></kml>